extends layout.pug

block content-header
  link(rel='stylesheet', type='text/css', href='/style/dataset.css')

block content-block
  .page-content
    h1 Data
    p The GNIS-LD dataset is a linked-data version of the USGS Geographic Names Information System. It describes every federally recognized place name in the United States. It is public domain, machine-readable, and available in bulk or live.

    h2 Download
    p Every release is archived as a gzip-compressed N-Triples file that can be loaded into any triple store. Releases are published quarterly.
    .vocab-actions
      a.btn-primary(href='/downloads') Download a release
      a.btn-link(href='/explore') Query it live instead

    h2 Documentation
    p The #[a(href='/docs') documentation] covers the URI structure, identifier stability and versioning, and the dataset's VoID/DCAT metadata. #[a(href='/docs#using') Using GNIS-LD] covers downloading releases, querying over SPARQL, and loading the data into pandas and PyTorch.

    h2#vocabularies Vocabularies
    p Two vocabularies, #[code usgs] and #[code gnis], describe the features in the dataset.
    .vocab-actions
      a.btn-primary(href='/vocabularies') Browse the vocabularies
